... later after adding receipt2 they check ledgerAfter.length > countBefore. But addReceipt doesn't create ledger entry. So expectation fails. Perhaps there is another place where receipt creation adds ledger entry via UI but not in test. Maybe they intended receiptStore.addReceipt to include ledger entry creation. So we need to modify addReceipt to appendEntryForReceipt('receipt.created', ...). Also for import test, they expect only imported entries, not receipt.created, because initLedgerIfNeeded runs after addReceipt? In import test they do addReceipt then addMileageEntry then initLedgerIfNeeded. If we add ledger entry on receipt creation, then initLedgerIfNeeded will import after receipt already added ledger entry, causing duplicate? They expect imports length 2, but also there would be receipt.created entries. But they filter imports kind 'imported', so fine. However ledger will have more entries. test later maybe expects length? Not checking.

