{
  "summary": "The UI implementation is generally well‑structured and follows the design tokens, component library, and accessibility guidelines described in DESIGN.md. However, the primary navigation (bottom tab bar) is not rendered or not reachable, causing the primary flow to break. Several required screen states (loading, empty, error) are missing or incorrectly wired, and a few accessibility details (focus‑visible outlines, ARIA roles, visible focus on the bottom tab bar) are omitted. The components use the theme tokens but there are several instances of hard‑coded colors, missing style classes, and missing touch‑target sizing. These issues prevent the app from satisfying the polished product bar.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/navigation/index.tsx",
      "issue": "Bottom tab navigator is never added to the UI; the BottomTabBar component is defined but not used, so the \"Dashboard\" tab cannot be clicked, breaking the primary flow.",
      "fix": "Wrap the main stack navigator in a BottomTabNavigator (e.g. createBottomTabNavigator) and include the BottomTabBar component as the tabBar. Ensure routes for Dashboard, Mileage, Settings, etc., are declared so the tab icons are rendered and testable."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The Accept button is enabled before the policy checkbox is checked, contrary to DESIGN.md which specifies it should be disabled until checked.",
      "fix": "Add a state variable tracking the checkbox status and set the Accept button's `disabled` prop accordingly. Use `primary` color token for the label and ensure the button displays the disabled style from the theme."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/components/ui/BottomTabBar.tsx",
      "issue": "The BottomTabBar component lacks ARIA `role=\"navigation\"` and visible focus styling (2 dp outline) for selected/unselected tabs, making it inaccessible for keyboard navigation and failing WCAG focus visibility.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityRole=\"navigation\"` to the container, and apply a focus‑visible style using `theme.colors.outline` and a 2 dp border when a tab receives focus. Ensure each tab item has `accessibilityState={{ selected: true/false }}` and a proper label."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing Loading state UI: the screen never shows a centered ActivityIndicator during data fetch as required by DESIGN.md.",
      "fix": "Add a conditional rendering that displays `<ActivityIndicator size=\"large\" />` centered with the copy \"Checking receipts…\" (or blank) while the receipt list is being loaded."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptHistoryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing Empty state UI: when a receipt has no history the screen should show the `EmptyState` component with title \"No changes yet\" and description \"This receipt has never been edited.\", but the code only displays a blank view.",
      "fix": "Render the `<EmptyState>` component with the specified copy and a primary \"Back\" button when the history array is empty."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptHistoryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Error handling is shown via a Snackbar only; the DESIGN.md expects the error to be displayed as a Snackbar but also to keep the screen accessible. The Snackbar currently lacks an `accessibilityLiveRegion=\"assertive\"` attribute.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLiveRegion=\"assertive\"` to the Snackbar component to announce errors to screen readers."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/VerifyExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Loading spinner for file reading does not display the required copy \"Reading file…\" and lacks role=\"status\" for assistive tech.",
      "fix": "Wrap the spinner in a view with `accessibilityRole=\"status\"` and include a `<Text>` element with the copy \"Reading file…\" to satisfy the design spec."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "FormField uses `TextInput` but does not set `error` state styling from the theme (e.g., red outline). Errors appear only via HelperText, violating the DESIGN spec's error state visual cue.",
      "fix": "Pass the `error` prop to `TextInput` and ensure the border color uses `theme.colors.error`. Also add `accessibilityState={{ invalid: true }}` when in error."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button's disabled state shows the primary text color (#0061A4) instead of the design token `color-on-disabled` (#212121), and the ripple effect remains visible on disabled buttons.",
      "fix": "Update the button style to use `theme.colors.onDisabled` for disabled label color and disable the ripple/elevation when `disabled` is true."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "EmptyState component uses a hard‑coded icon color and lacks the correct spacing (`spacing * 2` horizontal padding). It does not apply the design token `spacing-unit` for vertical gaps.",
      "fix": "Replace hard‑coded colors with theme color tokens (`theme.colors.onSurfaceVariant` for icon). Apply padding using `theme.spacing * 2` horizontally and vertical gaps using the base 8 dp unit."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/VerificationStatus.tsx",
      "issue": "The component does not include the required green check or red warning icons from the design tokens, nor does it announce the verification status via live region.",
      "fix": "Add `<Icon name=\"check-circle\" color={theme.colors.primary} />` for verified and `<Icon name=\"alert-circle\" color={theme.colors.error} />` for compromised. Wrap text in a view with `accessibilityLiveRegion=\"polite\"`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Screen component only includes `SafeAreaView` but omits the global `ScrollView` with horizontal padding of 16 dp defined in the DESIGN spec.",
      "fix": "Wrap children in a `<ScrollView contentContainerStyle={{ paddingHorizontal: theme.spacing * 2 }}>` to satisfy the layout."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/ReceiptCard.tsx",
      "issue": "ReceiptCard uses a hard-coded elevation value and background color instead of the theme's surface/elevation tokens.",
      "fix": "Apply `elevation={theme.elevation.level1}` (or appropriate level) and `backgroundColor={theme.colors.surface}`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/HistoryItem.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing focusable wrapper; list items are not keyboard navigable and lack a 2 dp outline on focus-visible.",
      "fix": "Wrap each HistoryItem in a `Pressable` with `android_ripple` and a focus-visible style using `outlineWidth: 2` and `outlineColor: theme.colors.outline`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/OfflineBanner.tsx",
      "issue": "Offline banner is present but uses a hard‑coded background color (`#FFEB3B`) instead of a token and does not respect the theme's `surfaceVariant`.",
      "fix": "Update the banner to use `theme.colors.surfaceVariant` for background and `theme.colors.onSurface` for text."
    }
  ]
}

